        "original_id": "371e8388-f762-51e6-8840-616b09b22570",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Guiping, Hailin, Guangxi, Heilongjiang, Mudanjiang, China\n- Rivers: Qian River, Yu Jiang, Xun, Xi Jiang, Hongshui River\n- Languages: Eastern Hongshuihe Zhuang\n- Concepts: county-level city, prefecture-level city, Northern Tai language\n\nFacts:\n- Guiping is a county-level city in eastern Guangxi, China.\n- Hailin is a county-level city in Heilongjiang province, northeast China, and it is part of Mudanjiang prefecture-level city.\n- At Guiping, the Qian River is joined by the more southerly Yu Jiang to form the Xun branch of the Xi Jiang.\n- Eastern Hongshuihe Zhuang is a Northern Tai language spoken in Guangxi, China, south of the Qian River and the eastern stretch of the Hongshui River.",
